**Question Title:** Simplify the Compilation Process

**Question Link:**  
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/9kh4giios2j4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg

**Solution:**
```bash
echo "#!bin/bash" > build.sh
echo "gcc hello.c -o hello" >> build.sh
chmod +x build.sh
gcc hello.c -o hello
./build.sh
./hello
```

**Approach:**

1. Adding the shebang line to the `build.sh` file to specify the script interpreter.
2. Compiling `hello.c` into an executable file named `hello` using GCC.
3. Giving execution permission to `build.sh`, then running the build script and executing the compiled program.

**Result:**

The program executes successfully and prints `Hello from C` on the terminal.